  "body": "Requested by the user (2026-11-11). The user's own machine is a Tormach 770MX, which uses **Tormach TTS** (Tormach Tooling System) holders: a 3/4 in straight shank in an R8/BT30-style spindle collet with a locating collar. Built-in TTS holders make CamCraft's own test jobs on that machine collision-accurate.\n\n**What:** built-in TTS holders as revolved profiles:\n- **TTS ER20 collet holder,** sharing the sibling ER-chuck issue's nut geometry;\n- **TTS Weldon (side-lock) end-mill holders,** in their common bore sizes;\n- **TTS face mill and shell mill arbor:** optional, if the dimensions are public.\n\nDimensions come from Tormach's public product pages and manuals, behaviour and dimensions only, recorded with sources. The gauge length is the TTS collar-to-tip length the tool setter measures, so it lines up with the machine's H offsets.\n\nEffort: high.\n\n**Done means:**\n- The TTS holders can be picked, and the 770MX machine file's tools can default to TTS.\n- Pinned by a test.\n- **Checked on the user's 770MX:** the modelled holder matches the real one closely enough for the collision checks; the user can measure.\n\nPart of #743.\n",
